# Task List Cursor Rules

## Project Structure Guidelines

### File Organization
- Keep related files in the same directory
- Use consistent naming conventions (kebab-case for files, PascalCase for components)
- Group components by feature or functionality
- Maintain clear separation between UI components, business logic, and utilities

### Component Guidelines
- Create reusable components in the `packages/ui/src/components` directory
- Use TypeScript for all new components
- Include proper prop types and interfaces
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Follow the existing component patterns in the codebase

## Code Quality Standards

### TypeScript
- Use strict TypeScript configuration
- Define proper interfaces for all data structures
- Avoid `any` types - use proper typing
- Use union types for better type safety
- Implement proper error handling with typed errors

### React Best Practices
- Use functional components with hooks
- Implement proper state management
- Use React.memo for performance optimization when needed
- Follow the single responsibility principle
- Keep components small and focused

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Follow the design system defined in `packages/ui`
- Maintain consistent spacing and typography
- Use CSS variables for theme customization
- Ensure responsive design for all components

## Development Workflow

### Git Practices
- Use conventional commit messages
- Create feature branches for new development
- Keep commits atomic and focused
- Write meaningful commit messages
- Review code before merging

### Testing
- Write unit tests for utility functions
- Test component behavior and user interactions
- Use React Testing Library for component tests
- Maintain good test coverage
- Test error scenarios and edge cases

### Performance
- Optimize bundle size
- Use code splitting for large applications
- Implement proper loading states
- Optimize images and assets
- Monitor and improve Core Web Vitals

## Documentation

### Code Documentation
- Document complex business logic
- Add README files for new packages
- Include usage examples for components
- Document API endpoints and data structures
- Keep documentation up to date

### Architecture Decisions
- Document major architectural decisions
- Explain design patterns used
- Record technical debt and future improvements
- Maintain architecture decision records (ADRs)

## Security Guidelines

### Data Handling
- Validate all user inputs
- Sanitize data before rendering
- Use proper authentication and authorization
- Implement secure API communication
- Follow OWASP security guidelines

### Environment Variables
- Never commit sensitive data to version control
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Document required environment variables
- Use different configurations for different environments

## Accessibility

### Web Accessibility
- Follow WCAG 2.1 guidelines
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Provide proper ARIA labels
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Test with screen readers

### User Experience
- Design for mobile-first approach
- Ensure fast loading times
- Provide clear error messages
- Implement proper loading states
- Use consistent UI patterns

## Monitoring and Logging

### Error Handling
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Log errors with context
- Provide user-friendly error messages
- Monitor application performance
- Set up alerting for critical issues

### Analytics
- Track user interactions
- Monitor application performance
- Use analytics to improve user experience
- Respect user privacy preferences
- Follow GDPR compliance guidelines

## Deployment and DevOps

### Build Process
- Optimize build configuration
- Use proper environment variables
- Implement CI/CD pipelines
- Run tests before deployment
- Use proper versioning

### Infrastructure
- Use containerization when appropriate
- Implement proper backup strategies
- Monitor system resources
- Set up proper logging and monitoring
- Plan for scalability

## Code Review Checklist

### Before Submitting
- [ ] Code follows project conventions
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] No console errors or warnings
- [ ] Documentation is updated
- [ ] Performance impact is considered
- [ ] Security implications are reviewed
- [ ] Accessibility requirements are met

### During Review
- [ ] Code is readable and maintainable
- [ ] Logic is correct and efficient
- [ ] Error handling is appropriate
- [ ] Tests cover the new functionality
- [ ] No breaking changes without proper migration
- [ ] Dependencies are properly managed

## Common Patterns

### State Management
- Use React Context for global state
- Implement proper state updates
- Avoid prop drilling
- Use local state for component-specific data
- Consider using state management libraries for complex state

### API Integration
- Use consistent API client patterns
- Implement proper error handling
- Use TypeScript for API responses
- Cache data when appropriate
- Handle loading and error states

### Form Handling
- Use form validation libraries
- Implement proper error messages
- Handle form submission states
- Provide user feedback
- Use controlled components

## Future Considerations

### Scalability
- Plan for application growth
- Consider microservices architecture
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use CDN for static assets
- Monitor performance metrics

### Maintenance
- Regular dependency updates
- Code refactoring when needed
- Performance optimization
- Security updates
- Documentation maintenance

